ProjectALife.DialogueShards["radio_18"] = {
{"r5_joke_birdie_grandson_nap","caller_joke",200,400,17,22,1,{"Caller - Birdie","Dee, I was watching my grandson, and he asked me why the dead ones never get tired","Dee","What did you tell him, Birdie?","Caller - Birdie","I said, well, honey, it's because they're dead","Caller - Birdie","And he said, 'Then why do I have to take a nap?'","Dee","That's a fair question","Caller - Birdie","So I told him, when you're dead, you can skip your nap too - his mama hasn't let me babysit since"}},
{"r5_host_marty_asleep_midsentence","host",200,400,19,23,1,{"Marty","The road from March Ridge to Ekron is clear as of this afternoon, clear up to the white church","Marty","Past the church, Travis says there's a car turned sideways, and you'll want to cut through the.. the","Dee","He's asleep, right there in the chair, mid-sentence - chin on his chest","Dee","I'm not waking him, he's been up thirty hours","Dee","I'll finish it for him - cut through the Tabor pasture, around the car, the gate's open, that's what he was going to say","Dee","We'll keep it down for a while, goodnight to everybody listening, from the one of us who's still awake"}},
{"r5_obit_marty_nolan_lake_gauge","obituary",200,400,8,21,1,{"Marty","A lot of you knew this voice, even if you never knew his name","Marty","Nolan Pryor, of Fallas Lake, every Friday since September, he called this station to report the level off the gauge on the boat dock - whether we asked or not","Dee","Mostly not","Marty","Mostly not - 'Marty, lake's at seven feet two inches, up an inch' and that was it, no goodbye, no favors asked","Marty","His neighbor came by the store to tell us, said Nolan wanted us to have his last reading, and he'd written it on a card - seven feet one inch","Dee","If somebody at Fallas Lake is near that gauge on a Friday, we'd take a reading - it doesn't have to mean anything","Marty","It's down an inch, Nolan, we've marked it"}},
{"r5_joke_tommy_marty_impression","caller_joke",200,400,17,22,1,{"Caller - Tommy","Marty, I do a real good impression of you, everybody at our camp says so","Marty","Let's hear it, then","Caller - Tommy","Ahem, good evening, folks - good evening, it is a fine, fine evening for salt","Dee","Oh no, oh, that's him - that is exactly him","Marty","I have never once in my life said it was a fine evening for salt","Dee","You said it last week, Marty, I wrote it down","Marty","Tommy, you've been a great help to this station - please don't call again"}},
{"r9_joke_d200_twenty_plenty","caller_joke",200,280,16,22,1,{"Caller - Lige","Breaker, nineteen - Marty, you got a copy?","Marty","Go ahead","Caller - Lige","What's your twenty?","Marty","I've got plenty","Caller - Lige","Plenty of what?","Marty","I don't know, son, you asked me","Caller - Lige","I asked where you're at","Marty","I'm at the feed store, I've been at the feed store nine months - where'd you think I was?","Caller - Lige","I'm going to hang up now","Marty","Ninety-nine point six, folks, we're a professional operation over here"}},
{"r9_host_d205_lige_arrives","host",205,260,0,23,1,{"Marty","There's a young fellow been sleeping in my hay barn about a week with my permission, and this morning he came in and made me an offer I want to read out loud","Lige","I'll sit up all night with the radio on so the both of you can sleep - that's it, that's the offer","Marty","And what do you want out of it?","Lige","A place out of the rain and whatever's in the pot - and to not be by myself at night, if I'm being honest about it","Marty","This is Lige, he drove a bread route out of Elizabethtown six years, up at two in the morning every working day of his life, so three o'clock don't mean to him what it means to me","Dee","I've told him the rules, he doesn't diagnose, he doesn't promise, he writes down everything and he wakes me for anything with blood in it","Lige","Write it down and wake the nurse, I got it","Marty","He gets the mic at eleven starting tonight - be decent to him, and if you're going to test him, test him on something easy"}},
{"r3_mb_d210_curtis_and_the_knob","music_bridge",210,320,0,23,1,{"Dee","My brother's here for the week, and he says he can make the transmitter reach farther - Marty says if he touches the knob that says 'DON'T,' he's walking back to Fort Knox","Curtis","Just looking at the knob, Marty- nobody's touching anything","Marty","He's looking at the knob","Curtis","Marty, this knob's not hooked to anything, the wire's cut - it's been cut for years","Marty","Put the cover back on, son, we'll be right back, folks - some things you leave alone"}},
{"r3_sf_d212_say_it_anyway","sign_off",212,261,22,23,1,{"Marty","Reverend Hollis is still sick at the parsonage, and Dee's still riding out there every other day on a bicycle in this cold, which I've told her is foolish","Dee","It is foolish","Marty","He asked her to ask me to say something in his place on Sunday - I told her I'm not a preacher, he told her to tell me he knows that, and to say it anyway","Marty","So here it is, and it's his, not mine - go home - eat something - be good to the people in your house - come back next week - good night"}},
{"r9_trade_d212_seed_corn_price","trade",212,280,9,16,1,{"Marty","There's a man in this county holding thirty bushel of seed corn and I'm going to read his price exactly as he wrote it, and then I'm going to shut my mouth about it","Marty","Two gallons of gas, or a box of shells, or four days of labor, for one bushel - meeting at his place, and he wants it known he's not alone out there","Dee","You said you'd shut your mouth about it","Marty","I did say that, so I'll let you talk","Dee","That's a hard price and it's his corn, that's both true, I'd rather he asked high and sold it than buried it in a barn where it does nobody a bit of good","Marty","There's one more thing in the note and it changes it some - he says four days of labor is for anybody, but a widow with kids pays him one day and he'll deliver it","Dee","Well, all right then","Marty","That's the Trading Post, key up if you want the road, and I'll give it to you the morning you go, not tonight"}},
{"r3_so_d215_glass_sleeves","sign_on",215,240,6,9,1,{"Marty","Morning - it's {time}, ice storm overnight, every limb in the county is wearing a glass sleeve, and they've been snapping all night - that's what the shots you heard were - mostly","Marty","Don't walk under trees today, don't walk at all if you can help it, a broken hip right now is a broken everything","Dee","I'm not joking about the hip","Marty","She's not, it's pretty out there, I'll give it that - stay inside and look at it through the glass, ninety-nine point six"}},
{"r3_mb_d215_ice_ticking","music_bridge",215,240,0,23,1,{"Marty","No music, but after this, if you're somewhere safe, step outside a minute and listen to the ice on the trees","Marty","When the sun gets on it, it ticks - Thousands of little ticks all through the woods, like every clock in the county started back up at once","Marty","It's ice letting go, I know, but I stood out there this morning and believed it was clocks for a minute - back in a bit"}},
{"r5_host_valentines_tow_chain","host",218,221,0,23,5,{"Dee","Somebody asked me if they could send a valentine over the air","Marty","We don't have a policy on valentines","Dee","We do now, the policy is yes","Dee","This first one's from R in Irvington to L in Brandenburg - it says, 'Still got the good scissors you swore I'd lose - haven't lost them - come see'","Marty","That's a long way to walk in February","Dee","Here's the second, 'to the fella with the tow chain on 31W back in October - you never gave a name, I think about your chain a lot'","Marty","Well, that's a very particular thing to think about a lot","Dee","Marty, let people be romantic about tow chains"}},
{"r9_host_d222_marty_reads_the_names","host",219,266,0,23,1,{"Marty","Reverend Hollis is at the parsonage with pneumonia and he's seventy-four years old, and that means somebody else reads the names on Sunday, and that somebody is me","Marty","I did it last week and I did it wrong - I read them fast, like a list, like a market report - four names in about thirty seconds and then I went straight to the weather","Dee","A woman called and told him so","Marty","She did, and she was right, and I want to thank her on the air for saying it to me instead of about me","Marty","So here's what I learned watching that old man do it for six months - he doesn't read a name, he tells you one thing the person did, and then he stops, and he lets it sit there a second before the next one","Marty","The stopping is the whole thing, I'm going to try to stop, Sunday, I'd appreciate your patience with it"}},
{"r9_obit_d219_marty_reads_them_wrong","obituary",219,219,8,12,8,{"Marty","It's Sunday and Reverend Hollis is at the parsonage with pneumonia, and I'm sat in his chair, which is my chair, which don't feel like my chair this morning","Marty","Last week I read the names too fast, so I'm going to go slow and if the silence bothers you, that's the point of it","Marty","Ardith Napier, of March Ridge, she ran the concession stand at the ball park and she would not let a kid go without a snow cone over a quarter - not one, in about fifteen years of it","Marty","Coy Sizemore, of Rosewood, he kept bees - forty-some hives, he told me one time that a man who works bees has to be in a good humor or they'll know it, and he said that was the best thing that ever happened to his temper","Marty","Delma Frye, of the Ekron road, who called this radio in November about her boy's inhalers, and who is not why I'm saying her name - I'm saying it because she brought me a pie in December and I never did thank her out loud","Marty","Thank you for the pie, Delma","Marty","That's three, I'd rather do three slow than eight fast - Reverend Hollis, if you can hear this over there, I did the stopping part"}},
{"r3_wx_d220_hog_wallow","weather",220,250,6,10,1,{"Marty","Weather - it's thawing, fifty degrees, and the whole county has turned to mud - every lane's a hog wallow","Marty","Good news, you can hear them coming now - Mud's loud, every step sounds like somebody pulling a boot out of a bucket","Marty","Bad news, you're loud too - walk the grass along the shoulder when you can","Marty","Rain coming in tonight, and a lot of it, with the snowmelt, the creeks will be up tomorrow - don't cross running water you can't see the bottom of"}},
{"r9_joke_d228_creek_cut_laugh","caller_joke",228,300,16,22,1,{"Caller - Lawson","Marty, I went in the creek Tuesday, all the way in, over my head, cold as it is","Marty","How'd you manage that?","Caller - Lawson","Bank give out from under me, fifty-eight years old and I come up looking like a drowned cat with my hat floating off downstream","Marty","You all right?","Caller - Lawson","Cut my leg on something down in there, didn't see what - could have been a piece of tin, there's tin all in that creek, heh","Caller - Lawson","Anyhow, it's a little warm around it today, I'll call you tomorrow either way, hahaha","Marty","Lawson","Dee","Lawson, what road are you on","Caller - Lawson","Aw, Dee, don't come out here in the dark","Dee","What road"}},
{"r3_so_d230_croup_and_harmonica","sign_on",230,330,5,7,1,{"Dee","Good morning - Dee, finishing up the night, overnight, a little boy with a cough on the Ekron road - his mother stayed beside him till morning","Dee","And a woman who couldn't sleep and wanted to talk about her garden for an hour - we talked about her garden for an hour","Dee","Scanner, nothing - CB, somebody playing a harmonica very badly around three in the morning - Leon, I know it was you, it was the fast version","Dee","Marty's coming on now, he's got his hat on backward, I'm not going to tell him - it's {time}"}},
{"r3_host_d230_eat_the_egg","host",230,330,0,3,1,{"Dee","Marty's asleep, so I'm going to talk about him, because he won't let me when he's awake","Dee","He hasn't taken a whole day off since last July - he gave his coat to a boy in January and wore two flannel shirts till I found him another - he eats last, I've watched him - he waits to see what's left","Dee","So if you come by the store with anything extra, a potato, an egg, you give it to me, not him - he'll just give it away","Dee","Don't tell him I said this, he wakes up sometimes and listens on the shop radio - Marty, if you're listening, eat the egg"}},
{"r9_host_d236_lige_composition_book","host",236,300,0,23,1,{"Marty","Something on my desk you can't see, so I'll describe it - black and white composition book, best thing in the building","Marty","Lige numbers every call, time, who it was, what they wanted, what he told them, and whether it needs somebody in the morning - last night was calls one hundred and four through one hundred and nineteen","Lige","I done it on the bread route, every stop, every count - if you don't write it you'll get to the fourth store and swear you already been","Marty","There's a column on the right I want to read out - he's got it headed CHECK ON, three names in it this morning","Lige","Two of them's the same woman two nights running, I don't like that","Dee","Then we'll ride out there today, that's what the column's for","Marty","A twenty-two year old bread man has organized this radio station better in three weeks than I did in seven months - say what you want about me, I know a good system when somebody hands me one"}},
{"r3_sf_d240_cans_before_people","sign_off",240,330,22,23,1,{"Marty","I'm tired tonight, I'm going to say so plain, since I've been saying everything else plain for most of a year","Marty","Some nights I count the diesel cans before I count the people - I don't like that about myself, I'm telling you so you'll check yourself for it too","Marty","People first, then the cans - count your people - good night"}},
{"r3_host_d240_river_carries_them","host",240,275,0,23,1,{"Marty","The river's up, the Ohio is out of its banks along the bottoms from West Point down past Brandenburg, and the Salt River's backed up behind it","Marty","If you're in Riverside or anywhere low, you already know - I'm saying it for the folks who don't live by the water","Marty","Nobody told us floods carry them - some of you have seen it, they come down on the current and fetch up in fence rows","Marty","So when the water goes down, walk the fence rows slow - look up in the brush - don't take it for granted that something hung up in a tree is done moving","Dee","And nothing the flood touched gets drunk - well, cistern, any of it - till it's boiled, settled, boiled again"}},
{"r5_host_geese_on_schedule","host",240,265,0,23,1,{"Marty","Geese went over this morning, headed north, loud as a school bus full of fifth graders","Dee","He ran out of the storeroom with one arm in his coat to look","Marty","I've watched the geese go over March Ridge fifty-some springs - I wasn't about to miss this one on account of a coat","Dee","They don't know anything happened down here, they're just keeping their schedule","Marty","Well, somebody ought to"}},
{"r5_trade_seed_swap_hazel","trade",240,290,9,16,2,{"Marty","It's seed time, so the Trading Post is a little different today - it's a seed swap","Marty","I've got field corn, sweet corn, and bush beans left from the store, and I'll give a handful to anybody who comes - out front of Colburn Feed, noon tomorrow","Caller - Hazel","Marty, it's Hazel Wimsatt, I've got cornfield beans my mamaw carried over the ridge in nineteen twenty-two - we've saved seed off them every year since","Marty","Hazel, those beans are worth more than my whole store","Caller - Hazel","I'll bring a coffee can full, I want tomato seed - anything but those hybrid ones that won't come true","Dee","Hazel, keep some of those beans back - don't give away the last of your mamaw's seed, no matter who asks","Caller - Hazel","Honey, I've got a quart jar buried under the smokehouse floor - I'm not a fool","Marty","Noon tomorrow, out front of the store - bring seed, take seed, and don't bring hybrids to Hazel"}},
{"r9_obit_d240_dee_reads_the_times","obituary",240,240,8,12,8,{"Dee","Marty's asleep and it's Sunday, so it's me, I've never done this and I'm going to do it my way, which is the way a nurse does it, so bear with me","Dee","Hettie Pruitt, of Rosewood, who wrote us a note in December that said she had nothing to trade and just wanted her name in the pile with everybody else's - she was seventy-one - Friday, about four in the morning, I was there","Dee","She asked me what day it was and I told her and she said, well, that's a Friday, and then she went back to sleep and that was all of it","Dee","Tilman Whitt, of West Point, nineteen years old - Tuesday evening, and I'm not going to say how, and don't any of you go asking his mother","Dee","He carried water to four houses on his street every day since October because none of them could carry it themselves - four houses - every day, nineteen years old","Dee","I write the times down 'cause somebody should know when, not only that it happened - odd reason, I know","Dee","Hettie Pruitt, Friday, four in the morning - Tilman Whitt, Tuesday evening, that's this week - Reverend Hollis, we're keeping your list for you"}},
{"r9_mb_d244_school_recorder","music_bridge",244,320,0,23,1,{"Marty","Tonight's music is a boy named Junior with a plastic recorder out of the fourth grade at West Point, and I want everybody to understand what we're getting into here","Marty","He's been practicing two weeks, his mother called and asked, and I said yes before I heard it","Marty","All right, Junior, whenever you're ready","Marty","That was the whole thing, he got to the end of it","Dee","He got to the end of it and he didn't stop in the middle - that's better than most of us managed today","Marty","Junior, you're on again Thursday, practice the part in the middle and don't let anybody tell you different"}},
{"r9_so_d246_bird_in_the_store","sign_on",246,300,6,9,1,{"Marty","Good morning, it's {time} and there is a bird in this building - been in here since yesterday evening, up in the rafters over the mineral blocks","Marty","A wren, she came in the dock door when Lige was hauling cans and she has no intention whatsoever of leaving","Lige","I propped the door and everything, she looked at the door - she stayed","Marty","So we're a bird store now - anything on the air today that isn't me is the wren, and she don't take requests","Dee","Leave her be, it's the first thing in this store all winter that came in because it wanted to","Marty","Count your people, and keep an eye on the wren"}},
{"r3_ins_d250_hand_on_the_dirt","instruction",250,300,5,12,1,{"Marty","Planting time, as best I remember it, the last frost around here comes about the middle of April - anybody who sets tomatoes out before then is a gambler","Marty","Peas, lettuce, onions, and potatoes can go in now, cold doesn't bother them, beans, corn, squash, tomatoes, wait till the ground warms, lay your hand flat on the dirt - if it's cold to the hand, wait","Marty","Plant extra - deer take some, rabbits take some, and whatever's left gets trampled by something that doesn't even eat it","Marty","And plant some of it so it doesn't look like a garden - potatoes out in the weeds, squash along a fence row, anybody passing by sees a pasture"}},
{"r3_mb_d250_peepers","music_bridge",250,290,19,22,1,{"Marty","Spring peepers, I'm holding the mic out the back door, those are the little frogs down in the flooded ditch - first night it's been warm enough","99.6 FM","(Hundreds of tiny frogs, high and constant, filling up the air)","Marty","Loud as they are, they hush the second anything walks past them - so if they quit all at once tonight, you listen harder - that's your music and your alarm in one"}},
{"r5_host_two_thousand_stay_safe","host",250,400,18,23,1,{"Marty","Evening, it's just me for the first bit - Dee's asleep, and I promised I wouldn't wake her for anything short of a fire","Marty","I don't have much tonight, the roads sound about the same as last week - Echo Creek is up over the low-water bridge","Marty","I sat down and figured it, and I've said 'stay safe' on this station something like two thousand times - I've wondered if it ever did one thing","Marty","Then a fella came by the loading dock last week and said he heard me say it on a truck radio outside Fallas Lake, and he turned around - didn't tell me why, just said he turned around","Marty","So I'm saying it again, two thousand and one - stay safe"}},
{"r9_sf_d252_lige_takes_it","sign_off",252,300,21,23,1,{"Marty","All right, this is the part I've been worrying about for two weeks, so let's get it done","Marty","I'm going to bed, this radio is not going off - Lige is sitting right there and he's got the mic from here till daylight","Lige","I'm on it, Marty","Marty","Anybody keys up tonight, that's who you get, and he knows more about being awake at three in the morning than I ever did - he did it for a living with a truck full of bread","Lige","Six years, loaf bread, sweet rolls and the little pies","Marty","Good night - go easy on that boy, he's twenty-two, and count your people"}},
{"r5_joke_leroy_undefeated_wildcats","caller_joke",255,300,17,22,1,{"Caller - Leroy","Marty, it's March, there ought to be a basketball tournament on","Marty","There ought to be, Leroy","Caller - Leroy","So I've decided - Kentucky won it all this year - undefeated, beat everybody by thirty","Marty","Big Blue, national champions","Caller - Leroy","And nobody can prove any different, that's the beauty of it","Dee","Anybody from Louisville who'd like to call in and argue, the lines are open"}},
{"r5_host_marty_never_gardened","host",255,300,0,23,1,{"Marty","I've tilled up the strip of grass between the store and the road - we're putting in a garden","Dee","Tell them how many gardens you've grown before this one","Marty","I've sold seed in March Ridge for thirty-one years","Dee","That's not what I asked","Marty","None, I have grown zero gardens, when a customer asked how deep to plant something, I'd turn the packet over and read them the back","Dee","He's out there right now with the seed packets lined up on the tailgate like a surgeon's tray","Marty","Folks with real gardens, call in, I'll trade salt for advice, and I'll act like I knew it all along"}},
{"r9_joke_d256_own_holiday","caller_joke",256,330,16,22,1,{"Caller - Newt","Marty, I've lost track of the holidays, so I've started my own","Marty","How's that work?","Caller - Newt","Every fourteen days I have a holiday, I don't name them, I just wake up and say, well, it's one, and then I don't do anything I don't have to","Marty","Does your wife go along with this?","Caller - Newt","She has her own, and hers are on different days, which I feel is the one flaw in the system","Marty","What do you do on a holiday?","Caller - Newt","Sit, and I'll tell you what, Marty, in thirty-one years at the plant I never once got a holiday I made up myself, so this is the best I've been treated by an employer"}},
{"r9_host_d258_three_shifts","host",258,320,0,23,1,{"Marty","We had a fight in this building last night, a real one, with a door slammed - I'm going to tell you what it was about because it's your radio too","Dee","It was about who sleeps","Marty","Dee wants the nights back, Lige won't give them up after six weeks, and I want them both home, but neither's got one","Lige","I said I'd take nights and Sunday both and they can have the rest","Dee","He's twenty-two, he'll say yes till he falls over - somebody in here has got to tell him no and it may as well be me","Marty","So here's what we settled on, and we wrote it on the wall by the door so nobody can pretend later - four on, eight off, three of us, same as a watch - and whoever's off does not come in this room","Marty","If you hear a tired voice on this station now, that's a person who broke the rule, and I'd like you to tell them so"}},
{"r3_host_d260_long_way_to_church","host",260,300,19,22,1,{"Marty","The redbuds are out on the ridge, purple all the way down to the creek, and the dogwoods coming on behind them","Marty","Nancy used to take the long way to church this time of year just to look at them - it added ten minutes, I'd complain about the ten minutes","Marty","I took the long way today - walked it, it added a lot more than ten minutes, and there wasn't anybody to complain to","Marty","Anyway, that was my walk, not a promise about your journey. Check for yourselves. I don't know what's on that road now"}},
{"r5_trade_roundup_spring_rototiller","trade",260,310,9,16,1,{"Dee","Spring Trading Post, read off the notes that came through the slot","Dee","A family in Echo Creek has twelve baby chicks, two weeks old - they want a roll of chicken wire, which is fair - Echo Creek low-water bridge, nine AM","Marty","A man in Irvington has a push plow, the old kind with the big iron wheel - he wants two gallons of gas, he says he sees the irony","Dee","Somebody in Rosewood has a box of seed packets off a hardware store rack - dated ninety-three, most will still come up - they want soap","Marty","The seeds are at the Rosewood courthouse steps, ten AM - the plow is at the Irvington post office, noon","Dee","And somebody's trading a rototiller that runs, they didn't say for what, they just wrote 'IT RUNS' and underlined it three times","Marty","If you're the rototiller, call in, you'll have forty offers by supper","Dee","Roads are muddy this time of year - leave early, and don't drive through water you can't see the bottom of"}},
{"r5_joke_kathy_tablecloth_wedding","caller_joke",260,400,17,22,1,{"Caller - Kathy","Dee, Marty, it's Kathy, from the wedding dress call - we did it, we got married","Dee","Kathy! Oh, honey - tell us everything","Caller - Kathy","Somebody brought a dress, a real one, size four - Dee, I haven't been a four since sixth grade","Marty","So what did you wear?","Caller - Kathy","A white tablecloth from the country club in Riverside, with a curtain rope for a belt - the preacher said I looked like a Roman","Caller - Kathy","Mike cried the whole time, he says it was the dust off the tablecloth","Dee","It was not the dust, Mike"}},
{"r9_ins_d262_mud_and_a_come_along","instruction",262,330,8,20,1,{"Marty","Spring mud, everybody's going to bury a truck this month and I'd like to cut that number down some","Caller - Orval","Marty, first thing - don't drive on a field or a lane you can't see the bottom of the ruts in - if somebody else's rut is deeper than your axle you're done before you start","Caller - Orval","And when you feel it going, get off it - don't spin, spinning digs you a hole shaped like your own tire and then you need three men and a jack","Marty","How about getting out?","Caller - Orval","Come-along and a chain, and hook to something that has roots - a live tree at the base, not a fence post, and not a stump you can rock with your hand","Caller - Orval","Wrap a coat or a chunk of carpet over the middle of that chain - if a hook lets go, the chain goes where it wants to, and a coat on it takes the snap out","Dee","And everybody stands out from the line, not beside it - not behind it holding the shovel, out from it, at the side, where the chain can't reach you","Caller - Orval","And boards - keep two boards in the bed year round, half the time it's boards under the back tires and you drive out like nothing happened"}},
{"r9_trade_d264_shoe_man_needs_leather","trade",264,340,9,16,1,{"Caller - Lonnie","Marty, I half-soled shoes in the back of the dry cleaner's at Muldraugh for twenty-six years - I can still do it, what I can't do is make leather out of air","Marty","What're you short on?","Caller - Lonnie","Leather, old boot tops, a saddle nobody's using, a truck seat, a purse, a belt, a coat - and rubber, a worn-out tire is a hundred soles if you've got the knife for it","Marty","And what do folks get?","Caller - Lonnie","Their shoes back with a sole on them, two pair for one good hide's worth, and I'll teach anybody who'll sit still, but I'll tell you now, it's a month of sitting still","Dee","Everybody listen to this part, the shoes on your feet are the shoes you have got - there is no store, a year from now this man is going to be the most important person in this county","Caller - Lonnie","I'm at the house behind the old dry cleaner's - bring the shoes and the leather both, and bring them dry","Marty","Behind the dry cleaner's at Muldraugh, daylight, and go look in your closets for the shoes you kept because they were too good to throw out - this is what you kept them for"}},
{"r5_joke_glen_daylight_saving","caller_joke",267,267,17,22,6,{"Caller - Glen","Marty, you setting your clocks forward tonight?","Marty","I hadn't planned on it, Glen","Caller - Glen","I'm doing mine - Congress passed a law, you don't just ignore Congress","Marty","What does your wife say?","Caller - Glen","She says, 'Glen, you go find Congress and bring him here, and I'll change the kitchen clock myself'","Caller - Glen","So I changed it while she was asleep, first law anybody's obeyed in this county since July"}},
{"r3_so_d268_easter_up_with_help","sign_on",268,268,6,9,10,{"Marty","Good morning, it's Easter Sunday, and I've got somebody back in the second chair who a lot of you have asked after since February","Reverend Hollis","Good morning, I'm told I sound like a gravel road - Dee says I'm not to talk longer than ten minutes, and she's standing right here holding her watch","Dee","Nine minutes now","Reverend Hollis","I had the pneumonia - I'm seventy-four, you can do the arithmetic - Dee sat up with me eleven nights, and the church brought soup till I couldn't look at soup","Reverend Hollis","So on Easter morning I'm not going to tell you about anybody getting up but me - I got up - slow, and with help, that's all I know about it this year, you get up with help","Marty","Reverend Hollis is back in the chair, everybody"}},
{"r5_obit_hollis_easter_hill","obituary",268,268,6,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, it's Easter Sunday, we'd have had a sunrise service on the hill behind the church at six, and I'd have forgotten my notes, same as every year","Reverend Hollis","I went up the hill anyway this morning, three people came, I don't know how they knew - I didn't tell a soul","Reverend Hollis","Nobody sang, we watched the light come up over the tree line toward Rosewood and didn't say a word, and it was the best service I've led in nineteen years","Reverend Hollis","This week's names are few, because it was a kinder week - I'm grateful for that","Reverend Hollis","Walter Ashby, of Riverside, who taught his whole street how to graft apple trees, so there'll be apples on that street for fifty years","Reverend Hollis","Lottie Mae Brown, of Muldraugh, who hid plastic Easter eggs with a nickel inside for the children on her street for forty years - her grandson found one in her gutter last week, from some year or other","Reverend Hollis","Happy Easter, whatever you believe, the sun came up over Rosewood this morning, and three people climbed a hill to see it - that's where I'll leave it"}},
{"r3_host_d270_morels","host",270,295,9,17,1,{"Marty","A spring question I actually know the answer to - Morels, yes, they're up - yes, under the dead elms and the old apple trees - no, I won't tell you where mine are, nobody in Kentucky has ever told anybody where theirs are","Dee","I have a medical note","Marty","Dee has a medical note","Dee","There's a false one that looks close - cut every one in half, long ways, a real morel is hollow all the way through, top to bottom - if it's stuffed with cottony stuff inside, throw it out - and cook them - never raw","Marty","And if a man offers to show you his morel patch, he's either lying or he's in love with you - probably lying"}},
{"r9_host_d270_beans_came_up","host",270,330,0,23,1,{"Marty","Everybody who called in and told me what to do with that strip of dirt out front, come out here and look at it","Marty","They came up, the beans came up - crooked as a dog's hind leg and about half the row's missing, and they came up","Dee","He has been out there twice an hour since Tuesday","Marty","I sold seed for thirty-one years and read the back of the packet to people and never one time put a thing in the ground - and I want to tell you what nobody told me, which is that it takes longer than you can stand","Marty","You put it in and then nothing happens for eight days and you decide you've done it wrong - that's the part they leave off the packet","Dee","Tell them about the sign","Marty","I've put a little sign on the end of the row with the date I planted them on it - so the next fool who does this can see how long eight days is"}},
{"r9_obit_d270_caller_recipe","obituary",270,400,8,21,1,{"Caller - Roxie","Marty, I want to read my mother and then I want to ask the whole county for something","Marty","Go on ahead","Caller - Roxie","Almeda Pruitt, of March Ridge, she took a jam cake to every funeral in this town for fifty years - every one, if you were kin to somebody in March Ridge you have eaten her cake","Caller - Roxie","And she never wrote it down, I asked her twice and both times she said she'd show me sometime","Marty","So what's the ask?","Caller - Roxie","Somebody in this county stood in a kitchen and watched her make it - I know they did, if that's you, I don't care if you only remember half of it - I'll take half","Marty","Almeda Pruitt, of March Ridge, and a jam cake, if you watched her make it, key up on nineteen, or write it out and put it in my slot","Caller - Roxie","Tell them it had blackberry in it and I'm nearly sure there was buttermilk - that's as far as I can get by myself"}},
{"r9_sil_d270_lige_asleep_pages","silence",270,350,0,5,1,{"Dee","Marty's asleep and Lige is asleep, and I've picked this up because it's been open about ten minutes and I didn't want anybody hearing dead air and worrying","Dee","He's got his head down on the composition book, pen still in his hand, twenty-two years old","Dee","I'm going to sit here and let him sleep and you can hear the pages moving when the fan comes round - that's all that is","Dee","If you need something, key up and I'll hear it - otherwise this is what the station sounds like tonight, and I think it sounds all right"}},
{"r9_joke_d272_photo_booth_strip","caller_joke",272,350,16,22,1,{"Caller - Roxie","Marty, I found a strip of them little photo booth pictures from the fair in eighty-nine in the bottom of a purse","Marty","Four little ones in a row","Caller - Roxie","Four of me and my sister making faces, and I've been looking at it two days and I want to report something","Marty","Go ahead","Caller - Roxie","I look better now","Marty","Roxie","Caller - Roxie","I'm serious, in eighty-nine I had a perm that I paid forty dollars for and it looks like a hat somebody sat on - I've hauled water up a hill for a year and I'd put myself up against that girl any day of the week"}},
{"r3_wx_d275_five_winters","weather",275,300,5,10,1,{"Marty","Weather, it's dogwood winter - every spring, right when the dogwoods bloom, one last cold snap comes through, and the old folks gave it a name","Marty","Down to thirty-three last night, frost on the low ground - if you set out tomatoes already, I told you you were a gambler - cover them tonight","Marty","There's redbud winter before this one, and blackberry winter after, in May - then locust winter, then my granddaddy's favorite, linsey-woolsey britches winter - and then it's summer","Marty","That's right - Kentucky gets five winters, that's a lot of winters for a state this size - high of sixty today"}},
{"r9_ins_d278_seed_saving_second","instruction",278,350,8,20,1,{"Marty","Seed saving, and this is for people who saved seed last fall for the first time and are now finding out which of it works","Caller - Vesta","Beans and peas will come true, so will tomato, and okra, and most anything that pollinates itself - save those and you get the same thing back","Caller - Vesta","Squash, pumpkin, cucumber, melon, any of them will cross with whatever was in the next row - you'll get something, you might not get what you planted, and you won't know till August","Marty","And the seed off a store-bought hybrid?","Caller - Vesta","You'll get about nine kinds of nothing out of it - it'll come up, it won't be the plant you liked, that's the one that breaks people's hearts in the second year","Caller - Vesta","Dry it hard, on a plate, in the shade, a week past when you think it's done - a seed put up damp will mold in the jar and you'll open it in March to a black mess","Caller - Vesta","And write on it - write what it is and the year and one word about how it did - ten years from now somebody's going to be reading your handwriting","Marty","That last part's worth a minute - write it like somebody's reading it in ten years, they will be"}},
{"r5_joke_phil_tax_day","caller_joke",279,281,16,22,5,{"Caller - Phil","Marty, I'm an accountant, it's April fifteenth, and for the first time in twenty-two years, I'm not up till midnight","Marty","Congratulations, Phil","Caller - Phil","Did my return anyway, habit - income, none - deductions, a house, a station wagon, a bass boat off my brother-in-law","Marty","Can you deduct a borrowed boat?","Caller - Phil","Marty, who is going to audit me?"}},
{"r9_obit_d282_hollis_lost_my_place","obituary",282,282,8,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, I've been back in this chair three weeks and I owe you an apology about the list","Reverend Hollis","While I was down with the pneumonia I lost my place - Marty kept names, Dee kept names, the church kept names, and there's about nine weeks in there where I cannot swear to you that everybody got read","Reverend Hollis","So I'm starting the whole list over from the beginning, from July, and I'll read four a Sunday until I've read every soul in this county again, and it'll take me the better part of two years","Reverend Hollis","I've been told that's foolish for a man my age - I've been told that by Dee, twice","Dee","Three times","Reverend Hollis","So this morning we go back to the start - Loyd Tipton, of March Ridge, who called the high school football games off a card table in the press box for fifteen years, and whose radio this is","Reverend Hollis","Every word any of us has said on this thing has gone out through Loyd Tipton's transmitter - there isn't a person listening who doesn't owe that man something - and I never once heard him call a game"}},
{"r9_host_d284_riverside_answers","host",284,350,0,23,1,{"Marty","Back in August I said on this radio that I had four marks in the ledger for Riverside and it had been bothering me - I said it and then I let it alone","Marty","Last night at about eleven a woman keyed up and said, is this the man that counts","Marty","There's forty-one people in a school building in Riverside - forty-one, they've had one radio the whole time and it only receives, and they have sat and listened to me for eight months without being able to say a word back","Dee","She said they know Wendell's name","Marty","They know Wendell's name, they know about Dolly and they know about the knob that says DON'T, and not one of them could tell me so until somebody hauled a transmitter over the ridge","Marty","I'm going to fix the ledger, it says four, it's going to say forty-five, and I'm going to leave the four crossed out where you can see it, because I want to remember what I didn't know"}},
{"r3_sf_d285_dolly","sign_off",285,300,22,23,4,{"Marty","Dolly passed this afternoon, the store cat, some weeks you heard more of her on here than you heard of me","Marty","She was asleep on top of the transmitter, where it's warm, and she didn't get up - eleven years old, that's a good long run for a feed store cat","Marty","I buried her out by the grain bin, under the antenna - Dee says that's sentimental - Dee helped dig","Marty","The top of the transmitter's still warm, I keep putting my hand on it - anyway - count your people - good night"}},
{"r5_trade_rosalie_sheep_shearing","trade",285,330,9,16,1,{"Caller - Rosalie","Marty, I've got fourteen ewes that need shearing before it turns hot, and my shearer's gone","Marty","I'm sorry, Rosalie","Caller - Rosalie","So I'm trading wool, anybody who helps me shear takes a fleece home - anybody who can spin gets two","Dee","That's wool socks and blankets next winter, everybody - think about next winter now, while it's warm","Caller - Rosalie","I've got hand shears, and I'll show you how, it isn't hard - it's just your opinion against a sheep's","Caller - Rosalie","The farm with the red barn on Fallas Lake Road, with a sheep painted on the mailbox - eight in the morning - bring gloves","Marty","Red barn, sheep on the mailbox, Fallas Lake Road, eight AM - bring gloves and a good attitude, the sheep won't have one"}},
{"r9_trade_d288_bees_split","trade",288,360,9,16,1,{"Caller - Amos","Marty, I've got nine hives and I ought to have twenty - they're going to swarm and leave whether I'm ready or not","Marty","So what's the trade?","Caller - Amos","I'll split a hive and give it to anybody who'll build me two boxes to my measurements and come help me work them three days","Marty","A whole hive of bees","Caller - Amos","A whole hive, and in two years you've got honey and you've got wax for candles, and your garden will do things you won't believe","Caller - Amos","But I'll tell you the truth up front, I need somebody who won't jump, a man who swats is worse than no man at all, and I've had two of those already this spring","Dee","And Amos, ask them the swelling question before you let them stand in your yard","Caller - Amos","I ask everybody now, the farm on the Fallas Lake road past the church, eight in the morning, and wear a long-sleeve shirt that buttons at the wrist"}},
{"r3_mb_d290_whippoorwill","music_bridge",290,380,20,23,1,{"Marty","There's a whippoorwill out behind the grain bin, it's been saying its own name for an hour without taking a breath - I don't have anything to play that beats it","Marty","My mother said if you heard the first whippoorwill of the year, you got a wish, as long as you never said it out loud","Marty","So I'm not saying it - back in a minute"}},
{"r3_sil_d290_nothing_in_the_room","silence",290,318,23,4,1,{"99.6 FM","(The carrier hums, nothing else in the room makes any sound at all)"}},
{"r9_sf_d290_lige_signs_off_ritual","sign_off",290,360,0,4,1,{"Lige","All right, that's me done - Marty's up in about two hours and he'll be a bear till the coffee","Lige","Tonight was sixteen calls, four of them was the same woman, which is fine, she can call sixteen times herself if she wants","Lige","Three names in the check-on column - Dee's got them and she'll go this morning","Lige","Same as every night, the bread truck's not coming, the phone's not ringing, and everybody I talked to tonight is still here - go to sleep"}},
{"r9_joke_d292_busiest_man_referrals","caller_joke",292,370,16,22,1,{"Caller - Elzie","Marty, I dug graves at the county cemetery eighteen years and I'd like to say I am the busiest man in Knox County","Marty","I believe you","Caller - Elzie","And every bit of my work is referrals, I've never had to advertise one day in my life","Marty","Elzie","Caller - Elzie","I'm going to say the other part before you say it - there's four of us doing it now and there used to be two, and the reason there's four is not good business","Caller - Elzie","But I'll tell you what I'd want said if it was me in there - I'd want it said that a man who knew what he was doing dug it, and that it was square, and that it was deep enough","Marty","They're square","Caller - Elzie","They're square, I'm the best in this county and there's nobody left who'd argue with me about it, so I'm claiming it"}},
{"r9_host_d296_silent_man_speaks","host",296,370,0,23,1,{"Marty","For about six months there's been somebody keying up in the mornings and not talking - click, a room, click, I've said good morning to that click two hundred times","Marty","Wednesday he talked","Marty","His name's Basil, he's out past Irvington - he's had a stroke in ninety-one and the words don't come the way he wants them, and he'd decided a while back that he wasn't going to sound foolish on a radio","Dee","Tell what he said","Marty","He said, good - morning - Marty, took him a while to get it out and I sat here and let him get it out","Marty","So Basil, same time tomorrow - you can click or you can talk and I don't care which, and anybody on nineteen who rushes that man will answer to me"}},
{"r3_host_d300_one_minute_welcome","host",300,400,0,23,1,{"Marty","A new family came up on nineteen yesterday, they came in through the woods from somewhere, and they asked me what they need to know - all of it, in one call","Marty","I've been at this ten months, and it turns out I could say it in about a minute","Marty","Quiet beats fast, daylight beats dark, water before food - don't walk toward a helicopter - say your name when you come up on somebody's place, and keep your hands where they can see them","Marty","The rest you learn or you don't, and I don't get a say - welcome to Knox County, folks... sorry, and glad you're here"}},
{"r3_ins_d300_six_babies","instruction",300,380,0,23,1,{"Dee","There are babies coming this summer, I know of six - I ain't joking, I'm keeping a schedule","Dee","If you're expecting, or somebody in your house is, come see me before the last month - I want to know how far along, what number baby, and whether the last one came easy","Dee","Get ready now, clean sheets you don't need back - clean string, or dental floss, and a pair of scissors you've boiled - two clean towels, and a warm place for the baby that isn't the floor","Dee","Most babies come fine on their own - most, what I'm for is the ones that don't, so when it starts, send somebody for me right then - don't wait to see how it goes, it goes faster than you think"}},
{"r5_host_derby_salt_block","host",300,302,15,20,5,{"Marty","First Saturday in May, about now there ought to be a horse race on the radio, and every soul in Kentucky ought to be quiet for two minutes","Dee","Marty's going to call one for us, he's been practicing in the storeroom - I've heard him","Marty","And they're off at Colburn Feed, salt Block breaks well and takes the rail, horse Wormer second, rabbit Pellets third, and Bicycle Horn far back and not trying","Dee","Bicycle Horn is a longshot, everybody","Marty","Into the far turn, it's Salt Block, holding, holding, because Salt Block does not move - at the wire, Salt Block by a length and a half","Dee","There's no mint julep, I found some mint behind the store and steeped it in warm water - it's terrible","Marty","Then it's a proper Derby after all"}},
{"r5_joke_vic_mosquitoes","caller_joke",300,390,17,22,1,{"Caller - Vic","Marty, I've found the one thing I envy about them","Marty","Go on, Vic","Caller - Vic","Mosquitoes won't touch them, not one bite","Marty","Well, that's something","Caller - Vic","It means every mosquito at Fallas Lake flies straight past three dead men to get to me - I'm the only restaurant still open"}},
{"r5_host_dee_charts_closed","host",300,400,0,4,1,{"Dee","Marty's asleep, it's me and Wendell and the chart box","Dee","I counted tonight, three hundred and forty charts opened since I came to this station","Dee","Ninety-six of them I've closed with 'doing better.' That was my resolution back in January - I've been writing it real neat","Dee","The rest, I don't know, some of the rest I do know, and I don't write that part down - I just close the folder","Dee","Ninety-six, that's a good number for a night like this - if you're one I don't know about, call in and make it ninety-seven"}},
{"r9_ins_d300_hornets_in_a_wall","instruction",300,375,8,20,1,{"Marty","Hornets in a wall, I've had four people ask me this week, and there's a right way and a loud way","Marty","The loud way is knocking the nest down in the daytime - I don't have to tell you how that ends, you'll be running and they'll be following and everything in the county will hear about it","Marty","Right way is after dark, cold if you can wait for it, and they're all home and slow - one person works, everybody else stands off and holds nothing but a light, and the light is not pointed at the hole","Dee","And before you do any of it, ask every single person in the house if they've ever swole up from a sting - not whether it hurt, whether they swole","Dee","If anybody has, you don't do this at all, and that person doesn't stand out in the yard to watch either - that's the one I can't fix out here","Marty","A ground nest you can drown in the dark with a bucket - a nest in a wall you seal the outside hole at night and leave the inside alone, and then you don't open that wall for a year","Marty","And if it's honeybees in that wall instead of hornets, you call me and don't you touch a thing - there's a man who will drive across this county for bees"}},
{"r3_so_d302_derby_day","sign_on",302,302,6,9,10,{"Marty","Morning, it's the first Saturday in May - in this state, that's Derby Day, and I'm not letting it go by","Marty","So here's the Derby, post time is whenever Dee finishes her breakfast - the field is Harlan's mule, the Greers' bay gelding, and a goat from the Ekron road that nobody's ever caught","Dee","I've got a dollar on the goat","Marty","Nobody's got a dollar that means anything, so bet a chore - Loser hauls water all week - it's {time}, they're in the gate"}},
{"r3_host_d303_hollis_coffee_cans","host",303,303,9,12,10,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, it's the second Sunday in May, which makes it Mother's Day - I thought about not bringing it up, then I thought about my mother, who'd have had something to say about that","Reverend Hollis","A lot of you lost your mother this year, a lot of mothers lost children, which is worse, and there's no day for it","Reverend Hollis","So I'm going to tell you what the children at the church did - Friday they went out and picked every wild thing blooming along the Rosewood road - Honeysuckle, fleabane, clover - put it all in coffee cans","Reverend Hollis","Nobody asked who each can was for, they just lined them up along the windowsill in the fellowship hall - twenty-some coffee cans, I've been looking at that windowsill all week","Reverend Hollis","If you've got a can, go put something in it"}},
{"r9_trade_d304_week_of_watch_for_a_tire","trade",304,380,9,16,1,{"Marty","This note is the first one I've read where the price is a person's nights, and I've thought about it a while, and I've decided to read it","Caller - Newt","I need one tire, fifteen inch, any tread on it at all, and I've got nothing left to trade but me","Marty","Say the offer","Caller - Newt","I'll pull your night watch a week, seven nights, ten till four, at your place, and you sleep the whole week through for the first time since last summer","Dee","Newt, a week of nights will take something out of you and you'll be two weeks getting it back - I want you to know that before somebody says yes","Caller - Newt","I know what a week of nights costs, it costs less than walking everywhere for the rest of my life","Marty","Then here's my piece of it, and this is me, not him - if you take this trade, you don't put that man on the fence alone the first night - you sit up with him one night and show him your place","Marty","Anybody with a fifteen inch tire and a bed they can't sleep in, key up - that's a real trade and I'd take it myself if I had the tire"}},
{"r5_host_bicycle_horn_taken","host",305,400,0,23,1,{"Marty","I have an announcement, the pink bicycle horn is gone","Dee","After seven years on that counter","Marty","A little girl came in this morning with her mama to trade eggs - walked straight up to the counter, squeezed it twice, and looked at me","Dee","She said her name was Kayla, age seven now, she's the one who drew the picture on the wall","Marty","So it's hers, I told her it was free, and she paid me an egg for it anyway, because her mama raised her right","Dee","He keeps reaching for the spot on the counter where it used to be - four times since lunch","Marty","Seven years, you get used to a thing"}},
}
